function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    var page := dval({source_page: ""})
    page["source_page"] = "capy-05-functions-and-closures"
    page["kind"] = "guide"
    page["slug"] = "functions-and-closures"
    page["route"] = "/doc/guide/functions-and-closures/"
    page["title"] = "5. Functions"
    page["content"] = "A function gives a name to a calculation. Parameters describe its input. The declared result type describes its output.\n\n## Define and call a function\n\n```capy\nfunction greet(name : string) string {\n    -> \"Hello, \" + name\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(greet(\"Ada\"), \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n**Output**\n\n```text\nHello, Ada\n\n```\n\nThe `->` expression supplies the function result. Use `return` when a function must finish early.\n\n## Parameters and defaults\n\nParameters have names and types:\n\n```capy\nfunction label(name : string, suffix : string = \"!\") string {\n    -> name + suffix\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(label(\"Capy\"), \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\n`label(\"Capy\")` uses the default suffix. Defaults are trailing literals. A direct call can omit them, but a function value keeps the full parameter list.\n\nCapy evaluates arguments once from left to right.\n\n## Overloads\n\nSeveral functions can have the same name when their parameter types differ:\n\n```capy\nfunction describe(value : s32) string { -> \"integer\" }\nfunction describe(value : string) string { -> \"string\" }\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(describe(42), \" \", describe(\"Ada\"), \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nThe argument types select the overload. A result type never selects one.\n\n## Conversion parameters\n\nA parameter declared with `as` permits one constructor conversion:\n\n```capy\nfunction show(value : as string) {\n    print(value, \"\\n\")\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    show(42)\n}\n\n```\n\n\nThe call behaves as if it passed `string(42)`. Capy does not chain several conversions.\n\n## Function values\n\nA function can be stored and called through a typed value:\n\n```capy\nfunction double(value : s32) s32 { -> value * 2 }\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var operation : function(value : s32) s32 = double\n    var answe"
    page["content"] = string(page["content"], "") + "r := operation(21)\n    print(answer, \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nA lambda defines a small function at its point of use:\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var add_one := function(value : s32) s32 {\n        -> value + 1\n    }\n    print(add_one(41), \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nA lambda can read captured outer values. Scalar captures copy. Array, `dval`, and struct captures share identity inside the workspace. A capture binding cannot be reassigned. The closure can mutate shared aggregate content.\n\n```capy\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var offset := 2\n    var values := [10]\n    var update := function() s32 {\n        values.push(20)\n        -> offset + length(values)\n    }\n    print(update(), \" \", values[1], \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\n## Generic and variadic functions\n\nAn `any` parameter creates a compile-time generic function. Use it when the same operation is valid for several concrete types.\n\nA variadic parameter collects values into a typed array:\n\n```capy\nfunction print_all(...values : as string) {\n    for value := values {\n        print(value)\n    }\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print_all(\"one\", \" \", \"two\", \"\\n\")\n}\n\n```\n\n\nUse `...items` to spread an array into a variadic call.\n"
    page["label"] = "5. Functions"
    page["capy_sig_lines"] = dval([])
    page["param_lines"] = dval([])
    page["notes"] = dval([])
    page["warnings"] = dval([])
    page["see"] = dval([{label: "4. Expressions and control flow", href: "/doc/guide/expressions-and-control-flow/"}, {label: "7. Arrays, tuples, and structs", href: "/doc/guide/collections-and-records/"}, {label: "print", href: "/doc/api/print/"}])
    page["examples"] = dval([])
    page["guide_examples"] = dval([{entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function greet(name : string) string {\n    -> \"Hello, \" + name\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(greet(\"Ada\"), \"\\n\")\n}\n", output: "Hello, Ada\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function label(name : string, suffix : string = \"!\") string {\n    -> name + suffix\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(label(\"Capy\"), \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function describe(value : s32) string { -> \"integer\" }\nfunction describe(value : string) string { -> \"string\" }\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print(describe(42), \" \", describe(\"Ada\"), \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function show(value : as string) {\n    print(value, \"\\n\")\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    show(42)\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function double(value : s32) s32 { -> value * 2 }\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var operation : function(value : s32) s32 = double\n    var answer := operation(21)\n    print(answer, \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var add_one := function(value : s32) s32 {\n        -> value + 1\n    }\n    print(add_one(41), \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function RENDER(request : dval) {\n    var offset := 2\n    var values := [10]\n    var update := function() s32 {\n        values.push(20)\n        -> offset + length(values)\n    }\n    print(update(), \" \", values[1], \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "", body: "function print_all(...values : as string) {\n    for value := values {\n        print(value)\n    }\n}\n\nfunction RENDER(request : dval) {\n    print_all(\"one\", \" \", \"two\", \"\\n\")\n}\n"}])
    component_render("/doc/components/doc_page.capy", page)
}
